{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And he sent him from the valley of Hebron.</b> Rashi explained: from the deep counsel of that righteous one buried in Hebron. The language of עֵצָה (counsel) and the language of עֲמוּקָה (deep) require explanation, for who counseled this counsel and what depth is in it? And what seems closest to me to say in this matter is as follows. For our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Genesis Rabbah 44:21): the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Abraham: 'How do you wish your children to be judged — in Gehinnom or in exiles?' And Abraham chose for himself the exiles. If so, this counseled counsel that Abraham counseled — to choose the exiles in place of Gehinnom, which is called 'deep Sheol' — for through this a question is resolved: when Israel sin, why does the Holy One, blessed be He, not judge them in their own land, and why does He exile them to the lands of the nations? Rather, because the exiles are in place of deep Gehinnom, therefore the just decree is to exile them מֵאִיגְּרָא רָמָא לְבִירָא עֲמִיקְתָּא — from a high roof to a deep pit, for the land of Israel is higher than all lands, and relative to it all other lands are deep. This is what it says (Genesis 45:9): ״רְדָה אֵלַי אַל תַּעֲמֹד״ — 'come down to me, do not stand' — for when they went down to Egypt they went by way of descent, like one descending to deep Sheol, and this stands in place of deep Sheol for them. This is what it says: 'from the deep counsel of that righteous one' — for he counseled to choose the depth of the lands of the nations, as stated."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:32:14.364480056Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}